by chalasr at 2025-01-04T19:35:35Z

Some changes have been pushed:
- The special `invokable: true` attribute initially added to the `console.command` DI tag was removed in favor of relying on method-existence detection in the compiler pass.
- The `InvokableCommand` internal wrapper is now really callable, which makes `TraceableCommand` work with invokable commands.
-  Invokable commands can get the `Application` instance as argument if their signature ask for it, instead of the `Command` instance initially proposed.
- More tests were added.

My thoughts on previous discussions and limitations regarding regular commands:
- I agree with most concerns shared in https://github.com/symfony/symfony/pull/59340#issuecomment-2567283033 about supporting `AsCommand` on any public method, though part of them could be mitigated with some DX mesures and I think it would be nice to make it work later. Let's keep it simple on this iteration which is a huge game-changer already.
- I don't mind not having `initialize()` and `interact()` equivalents for invokable commands. Although there are some usages out there, most could work as well without them. Moreover they just don't fit with the invokable command principle conceptually.

The patch is super straightforward, and opens a lot of doors. Also the feature can be adopted by any Console-dependent package with a bit of DI glue since the implementation relies on the existing infrastructure (`setCode()`). I like this a lot.

